WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.180
Ryan Reynolds is one sneaky rascal.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:07.580
In response to a fan on Twitter asking whether
it was okay to screen Reynolds' hit Deadpool

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.880
for his four-year old, the star offered a
bit of tongue-in-cheek advice: lie your face

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.380
off, a tack he claimed to have taken with
his own daughters.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:20.000
Reynolds is known far and wide for two things:
inhabiting the character of Deadpool to an

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.460
extent which may not exactly be healthy, and
his Twitter feed, which is one of the greatest

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.180
compendiums of hilarity on the entire internet,
at least according to his superfans.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:33.760
The latest example of this was prompted by
Twitter user @jediminndtrick, who asked:

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.660
"RYAN I HAVE AN IMPORTANT QUESTION I NEED
AN ANSWER TO RIGHT TF NOW!!!

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.840
My son is 4, he loves Marvel, I'm dying to
show him Deadpool but I can't decide if I

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:42.680
should or not.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:43.820
Helpasistahout!!!!!!!!"

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:48.680
Reynolds immediately leaped into action, doubtless
convinced by all of those caps that this was,

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.660
indeed, a question that needed to be answered
with all due haste.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.360
His advice was as awesome as it was hilariously
irresponsible:

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:56.200
"No.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.460
Put on Spider-Man (from 2002) and tell him
it's Deadpool.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:00.820
It's what I do with my kids.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.040
Remember to look him straight in the eye when
you lie.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:03.800
Good luck."

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:09.979
So, apparently, Reynolds' children, 4-year-old
James and 2-year-old Ines, seen here in 2016,

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:13.700
think he is Spider-Man, which is a pretty
neat trick, if you ask us.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:17.560
Sure, there are a few similarities between
the costumes of the wall-crawler and the Merc

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.790
with a Mouth, but how on Earth does Reynolds
explain why he looks exactly like Tobey Maguire

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.140
when the mask comes off?

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.540
We knew kids could be gullible, but that's
just ridiculous.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:31.000
Of course, a quick perusal of Reynolds' previous
tweets quickly reveal that his musings on

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.480
parenting, and well, most topics, are never,
ever, to be taken seriously.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:37.680
Here's a quick selection of our favorites:

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.800
"My daughter's only 6 months old and already
drawing.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.000
I'd hang it on the fridge but honestly, it's
absolute garbage."

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:47.660
"I'm teaching my daughter that the sun goes
down each night because it's mad at her.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.940
Probably gonna write a book on parenting at
some point."

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.760
And, our all-time favorite:

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.600
"Totally caved and tossed my daughter the
keys to the car.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.000
She looked really happy as they bounced off
her tiny infant face."

00:01:58.369 --> 00:02:03.399
Obviously, Reynolds is a guy who loves his
family and screwing with people in equal measure.

00:02:03.399 --> 00:02:08.050
Soon, he'll have another unsuspecting youngster
to torment: he and his wife Blake Lively are

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.340
expecting their third child any old time now.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:14.160
Little does the new arrival know that it's
going to have Deadpool…er, Spider-Man…for

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.340
a dad.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:19.160
Reynolds had better hope that his children
never have occasion to meet Tobey Maguire,

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.680
or they're going to have a lot of uncomfortable
questions.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.640
At any rate, the cinematic fate of Deadpool
is still very much up in the air following

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:29.540
Disney's acquisition of the film and television
assets of Fox Studios.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.580
Although it's understandable that the character's
R-rated antics might be a tough fit for the

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:39.190
Marvel Cinematic Universe, 2016's Deadpool
and 2018's Deadpool 2 combined to rake in

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:44.870
over $1.5 billion dollars worldwide, and the
House of Mouse is unlikely to put such a proven

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:46.460
cash cow out to pasture.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:50.920
The rumor mill insists that not only is Deadpool
3 in the works, but that there are plans to

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:55.790
weave the character into the fabric of the
MCU by way of multiple cameos in Marvel Studios'

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.780
upcoming films and television series.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:02.400
Unfortunately, with talks between Marvel and
Sony Pictures having recently broken down,

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.180
it's looking increasingly likely that fans
will never get to see the onscreen pairing

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:10.440
that once seemed inevitable: Reynolds' Deadpool
and Tom Holland's Spider-Man.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.040
"You don't even know he looks like.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.180
What if he's like, seriously burned?"

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:15.260
"I wouldn't care.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.040
I would still love him for the person he is
on the inside."

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.520
Then again, from Reynolds' point of view,
this might be a good thing.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.480
When his kids get a little bit older, perhaps
he can show them Spider-Man: Homecoming, or,

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.660
as we call it, "Deadpool in high school."

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.860
"They let you throw parties, you know?

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.640
My parents are...dead."

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.720
Boy, are those kids ever going to grow up
confused.

